     [FeatureAccum16]>;
+
+// #320 Inc 4 Ph2: off-by-default far-pointer calling-convention variants. Each
+// selects HOW a 32-bit far (addrspace 2) pointer is passed/returned across a
+// call. Like FeatureAccum16, NONE is attached to any Family in MOSDevices.td, so
+// default mosw65816 codegen is byte-identical; the A-B measurement harness
+// selects one via -target-feature (e.g. +mos-farcc-imag32). farPtrCC() reads the
+// first one set; with none set, a far pointer crossing a call still errors as it
